  "paper_id": "ccs-2025-from-ot-to-ole-with-subquadratic-communication-1b65f402",
  "title": "From OT to OLE with Subquadratic Communication",
  "abstract": "Oblivious Linear Evaluation (OLE) is an algebraic generalization of oblivious transfer (OT) that forms a critical part of a growing number of applications. An OLE protocol over a modulus q enables the receiver party to securely evaluate a line a⋅ X+b chosen by the sender party on a secret point x∈ ℤq. Motivated by the big efficiency gap between OLE and OT and by fast OT extension techniques, we revisit the question of reducing OLE to OT, aiming to improve the communication cost of known reductions.",
